{"1-2":{"people":[{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"nebuchadnezzar-h5019","name":"Nebuchadnezzar","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Belshazzar","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"baanah-h1196i","name":"Baanah","kind":"person","brief":"Returned leader","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"bigvai-h0902g","name":"Bigvai","kind":"person","brief":"Returned leader","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"bilshan-h1114","name":"Bilshan","kind":"person","brief":"Returned leader","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"joshua-h3091j","name":"Joshua","kind":"person","brief":"A High Priest","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"mispar-h4558","name":"Mispar","kind":"person","brief":"Returned from exile","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"mordecai-h4782g","name":"Mordecai","kind":"person","brief":"Returned leader","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"nehemiah-h5166g","name":"Nehemiah","kind":"person","brief":"Returned leader","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"reelaiah-h7480","name":"Reelaiah","kind":"person","brief":"Returned leader","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"rehum-h7348a","name":"Rehum","kind":"person","brief":"Returned leader","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"seraiah-h8304l","name":"Seraiah","kind":"person","brief":"Returned priest","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"zerubbabel-h2216","name":"Zerubbabel","kind":"person","brief":"Governor","count":1,"firstVerse":2}],"places":[{"id":"babylon-h0894","name":"Babylon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":1}],"words":[{"base":"H0894","lemma":"בָּבֶ֫ל, בָּבֶל","tr":"ba·vel","gloss":"Babylon","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":262},{"base":"H1114","lemma":"בִּלְשָׁן","tr":"bil·shan","gloss":"Bilshan","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H0902","lemma":"בִּגְוַי","tr":"big·vay","gloss":"Bigvai","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"H5166","lemma":"נְחֶמְיָה","tr":"ne·chem·yah","gloss":"Nehemiah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"H7348","lemma":"רְחוּם","tr":"re·chum","gloss":"Rehum","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"H1196","lemma":"בַּעֲנָה","tr":"ba·a·nah","gloss":"Baanah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":9},{"base":"H8304","lemma":"שְׂרָיָהוּ","tr":"se·ra·yah","gloss":"Seraiah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":20},{"base":"H2216","lemma":"זְרֻבָּבֶ֫ל","tr":"ze·rub·ba·vel","gloss":"Zerubbabel","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":21},{"base":"H3442","lemma":"יֵשׁוּעַ","tr":"ye·shu·a","gloss":"Jeshua","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":29},{"base":"H1473","lemma":"גּוֹלָה","tr":"go·lah","gloss":"captivity","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":43}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2KI","chapter":24,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"He carried into exile all Jerusalem—all the commanders and mighty men of valor, all the craftsmen and metalsmiths—ten thousand captives in all. Only the poorest people of the land remained.","from":1},{"book":"2KI","chapter":24,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"The king of Babylon also brought into exile to Babylon all seven thousand men of valor and a thousand craftsmen and metalsmiths—all strong and fit for battle.","from":1},{"book":"2KI","chapter":25,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Then Nebuzaradan captain of the guard carried into exile the people who remained in the city, along with the deserters who had defected to the king of Babylon and the rest of the population.","from":1},{"book":"2KI","chapter":24,"verse":14,"verseEnd":16,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"He carried into exile all Jerusalem—all the commanders and mighty men of valor, all the craftsmen and metalsmiths—ten thousand captives in all. Only the poorest people of the land remained. Nebuchadnezzar carried away Jehoiachin to Babylon, as well as the kingʼs mother, his wives, his officials, and the leading men of the land. He took them into exile from Jerusalem to Babylon. The king of Babylon also brought into exile to Babylon all seven thousand men of valor and a thousand craftsmen and metalsmiths—all strong and fit for battle.","from":1},{"book":"2CH","chapter":36,"verse":1,"verseEnd":23,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then the people of the land took Jehoahaz son of Josiah and made him king in Jerusalem in place of his father. Jehoahaz was twenty-three years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem three months. And the king of Egypt dethroned him in Jerusalem and imposed on Judah a levy of a hundred talents of silver and a talent of gold. Then Neco king of Egypt made Eliakim brother of Jehoahaz king over Judah and Jerusalem, and he changed Eliakimʼs name to Jehoiakim. But Neco took Eliakimʼs brother Jehoahaz and carried him off to Egypt. Jehoiakim was twenty-five years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem eleven years. And he did evil in the sight of the LORD his God.","from":1},{"book":"EZR","chapter":1,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"In all, there were 5,400 gold and silver articles. Sheshbazzar brought all these along when the exiles went up from Babylon to Jerusalem.","from":2},{"book":"EZR","chapter":3,"verse":8,"verseEnd":9,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"In the second month of the second year after they had arrived at the house of God in Jerusalem, Zerubbabel son of Shealtiel, Jeshua son of Jozadak, and the rest of their associates including the priests, the Levites, and all who had returned to Jerusalem from the captivity, began the work. They appointed Levites twenty years of age or older to supervise the construction of the house of the LORD. So Jeshua and his sons and brothers, Kadmiel and his sons (descendants of Yehudah), and the sons of Henadad and their sons and brothers—all Levites—joined together to supervise those working on the house of God.","from":2},{"book":"EZR","chapter":4,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"But Zerubbabel, Jeshua, and the other heads of the families of Israel replied, “You have no part with us in building a house for our God, since we alone must build it for the LORD, the God of Israel, as Cyrus king of Persia has commanded us.”","from":2}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"persian-era","title":"Persian era: Esther and the return","people":2},{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":2},{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"3-35":{"people":[{"id":"parosh-h6551g","name":"Parosh","kind":"person","brief":"Returned from exile","count":1,"firstVerse":3},{"id":"shephatiah-h8203l","name":"Shephatiah","kind":"person","brief":"Returned from exile","count":1,"firstVerse":4},{"id":"arah-h0733h","name":"Arah","kind":"person","brief":"Nehemiah's opponent","count":1,"firstVerse":5},{"id":"jeshua-h3442i","name":"Jeshua","kind":"person","brief":"Returned leader","count":1,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"joab-h3097i","name":"Joab","kind":"person","brief":"Returned from exile","count":1,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"pahath-moab-h6355g","name":"Pahath-moab","kind":"person","brief":"Returned from exile","count":1,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"elam-h5867b","name":"Elam","kind":"person","brief":"Returned from exile","count":2,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"zattu-h2240g","name":"Zattu","kind":"person","brief":"Returned divorcee","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"zaccai-h2140","name":"Zaccai","kind":"person","brief":"Returned from exile","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"bani-h1137q","name":"Bani","kind":"person","brief":"Returned from exile","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"bebai-h0893g","name":"Bebai","kind":"person","brief":"Returned leader","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"azgad-h5803g","name":"Azgad","kind":"person","brief":"Returned from exile","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"adonikam-h0140","name":"Adonikam","kind":"person","brief":