ss":"Besai","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H1213","lemma":"בַּצְלוּת","tr":"bats·lut","gloss":"Bazluth","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H1227","lemma":"בַּקְבּוּק","tr":"baq·buq","gloss":"Bakbuk","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H1302","lemma":"בַּרְקוֹס","tr":"bar·qos","gloss":"Barkos","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H1502","lemma":"גַּזָּם","tr":"gaz·zam","gloss":"Gazzam","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H1515","lemma":"גַּ֫חַר","tr":"ga·char","gloss":"Gahar","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1CH","chapter":9,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Now the first to resettle their own property in their cities were Israelites, priests, Levites, and temple servants.","from":43},{"book":"1CH","chapter":9,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Now the first to resettle their own property in their cities were Israelites, priests, Levites, and temple servants.","from":58},{"book":"JOS","chapter":9,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"They continued, “Let them live, but let them be woodcutters and water carriers for the whole congregation.” So the leaders kept their promise.","from":58},{"book":"JOS","chapter":9,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Now therefore you are under a curse and will perpetually serve as woodcutters and water carriers for the house of my God.”","from":58},{"book":"JOS","chapter":9,"verse":27,"verseEnd":27,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"On that day he made them woodcutters and water carriers, as they are to this day for the congregation of the LORD and for the altar at the place He would choose.","from":58},{"book":"1KI","chapter":9,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"their descendants who remained in the land, those whom the Israelites were unable to devote to destruction—Solomon conscripted these people to be forced laborers, as they are to this day.","from":55},{"book":"1KI","chapter":9,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"their descendants who remained in the land, those whom the Israelites were unable to devote to destruction—Solomon conscripted these people to be forced laborers, as they are to this day.","from":58},{"book":"EZR","chapter":7,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So in the seventh year of King Artaxerxes, he went up to Jerusalem with some of the Israelites, including priests, Levites, singers, gatekeepers, and temple servants.","from":58}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"59-63":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":59},{"id":"delaiah-h1806i","name":"Delaiah","kind":"person","brief":"Returned from exile","count":1,"firstVerse":60},{"id":"nekoda-h5353h","name":"Nekoda","kind":"person","brief":"Returned priest","count":1,"firstVerse":60},{"id":"tobiah-h2900h","name":"Tobiah","kind":"person","brief":"Returned from exile","count":1,"firstVerse":60},{"id":"barzillai-h1271g","name":"Barzillai","kind":"person","brief":"David's compatriot","count":1,"firstVerse":61},{"id":"barzillai-h1271i","name":"Barzillai","kind":"person","brief":"Returned priest","count":1,"firstVerse":61},{"id":"habaiah-h2252","name":"Habaiah","kind":"person","brief":"Returned priest","count":1,"firstVerse":61},{"id":"hakkoz-h6976i","name":"Hakkoz","kind":"person","brief":"Returned priest","count":1,"firstVerse":61}],"places":[{"id":"addan-h0135","name":"Addan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":59},{"id":"cherub-h3743","name":"Cherub","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":59},{"id":"immer-h0564i","name":"Immer","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":59},{"id":"tel-harsha-h8521","name":"Tel-harsha","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":59},{"id":"tel-melah-h8528","name":"Tel-melah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":59},{"id":"gilead-h1568g","name":"Gilead","kind":"place","brief":"In Manasseh","count":1,"firstVerse":61}],"words":[{"base":"H8521","lemma":"תֵּל חַרְשָׁא","tr":"tel char·sah","gloss":"Tel-harsha","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":4},{"base":"H8528","lemma":"תֵּל מֶ֫לַח","tr":"tel me·lach","gloss":"Tel-melah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":4},{"base":"H1271","lemma":"בַּרְזִלַּי","tr":"bar·zil·lay","gloss":"Barzillai","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":12},{"base":"H2252","lemma":"חֲבַיָה","tr":"cha·vay·yah","gloss":"Habaiah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H3743","lemma":"כְּרוּב","tr":"ke·ruv","gloss":"Cherub","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H6944","lemma":"קֹ֫דֶשׁ","tr":"qo·desh","gloss":"holiness","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":469},{"base":"H5353","lemma":"נְקוֹדָא","tr":"ne·qo·da","gloss":"Nekoda","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H8550","lemma":"תֻּמִּים","tr":"tum·mim","gloss":"Thummim","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H8660","lemma":"תִּרְשָׁתָא","tr":"tir·sha·ta","gloss":"governor","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H6976","lemma":"קוֹץ","tr":"qots","gloss":"Koz","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2SA","chapter":17,"verse":27,"verseEnd":27,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"When David came to Mahanaim, he was met by Shobi son of Nahash from Rabbah of the Ammonites, Machir son of Ammiel from Lo-debar, and Barzillai the Gileadite from Rogelim.","from":61},{"book":"EXO","chapter":28,"verse":30,"verseEnd":30,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And place the Urim and Thummim in the breastpiece of judgment, so that they will also be over Aaronʼs heart whenever he comes before the LORD. Aaron will continually carry the judgment of the sons of Israel over his heart before the LORD.","from":63},{"book":"LEV","chapter":2,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The remainder of the grain offering shall belong to Aaron and his sons; it is a most holy part of the food offerings to the LORD.","from":63},{"book":"LEV","chapter":2,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"But the remainder of the grain offering shall belong to Aaron and his sons; it is a most holy part of the food offerings to the LORD.","from":63},{"book":"LEV","chapter":6,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"It must not be baked with leaven; I have assigned it as their portion of My food offerings. It is most holy, like the sin offering and the guilt offering.","from":63},{"book":"LEV","chapter":6,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Any male among the priests may eat it; it is most holy.","from":63},{"book":"LEV","chapter":7,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"If, however, the sacrifice he offers is a vow or a freewill offering, it shall be eaten on the day he presents his sacrifice, but the remainder may be eaten on the next day.","from":63},{"book":"LEV","chapter":8,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then he put the breastpiece on him and placed the Urim and Thummim in the breastpiece.","from":63}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"64-67":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H3967","lemma":"מֵאָה","tr":"me·ah","gloss":"hundred","lang":"h","inPassage":7,"uses":581},{"base":"H7651","lemma":"שֶׁ֫בַע","tr":"she·va","gloss":"seven","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":394},{"base":"H7970","lemma":"שְׁלֹשִׁים","tr":"she·lo·shim","gloss":"thirty","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":172},{"base":"H0505","lemma":"אֶ֫לֶף","tr":"e·leph","gloss":"thousand","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":506},{"base":"H7891","lemma":"שִׁיר","tr":"shir","gloss":"to sing","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":87},{"base":"H8337","lemma":"שֵׁשׁ","tr":"shesh","gloss":"six","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":216},{"base":"H0702","lemma":"אַרְבַּע","tr":"ar·ba","gloss":"four","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":318},{"base":"H2568","lemma":"חָמֵשׁ","tr":"cha·mesh","gloss":"five","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":343},{"base":"H7969","lemma":"שָׁלֹשׁ","tr":"sha·losh","gloss":"three","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":431},{"base":"H7239","lemma":"רִבּוֹ","tr":"rib·bo","gloss":"ten thousand","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":10}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"EXO","chapter":15,"verse":20,"verseEnd":21,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then Miriam the prophetess, Aaronʼs sister, took a tambourine in her hand, and all the women followed her with tambourines and dancing. And Miriam sang back to them: “Sing to the LORD, for He is highly exalted; the horse and rider He has thrown into the sea.”","from":65},{"book":"2SA","chapter":19,"verse":35,"verseEnd":35,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"I am now eighty years old. Can I discern what is good and what is not? Can your servant taste what he eats or drinks? Can I still hear the voice of singing men and women? Why should your servant be an added burden to my lord the king?","from":65},{"book":"EZR","chapter":9,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"But now, for a brief moment, grace has come from the LORD our God to preserve for us a remnant and to give us a stake in His holy place. Even in our bondage, our God has given us new life and light to our eyes.","from":64},{"book":"NEH","chapter":7,"verse":66,"verseEnd":69,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The whole assembly numbered 42,360, in addition to their 7,337 menservants and maidservants, as well as their 245 male and female singers. They had 736 horses, 245 mules, 435 camels, and 6,720 donkeys.","from":64},{"book":"NEH","chapter":7,"verse":67,"verseEnd":67,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"in addition to their 7,337 menservants and maidservants, as well as their 245 male and female singers.","from":65},{"book":"PSA","chapter":68,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The singers lead the way, the musicians follow after, among the maidens playing tambourines.","from":65},{"book":"PSA","chapter":148,"verse":12,"verseEnd":13,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"young men and maidens, old and young together. Let them praise the name of the LORD, for His name alone is exalted; His splendor is above the earth and the heavens.","from":65},{"book":"ECC","chapter":2,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"and I accumulated for myself silver and gold and the treasure of kings and provinces. I gathered to myself male and female singers, and the delights of the sons of men—many concubines.","from":65}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"68-70":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":70},{"id":"levi-h3878","name":"Levi","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":70}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":68}],"words":[{"base":"H1871","lemma":"דַּרְכְּמוֹן","tr":"dar·ke·mon","gloss":"drachma","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H0505","lemma":"אֶ֫לֶף","tr":"e·leph","gloss":"thousand","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":506},{"base":"H4488","lemma":"מָנֶה","tr":"ma·neh","gloss":"mina","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H3548","lemma":"כֹּהֵן","tr":"ko·hen","gloss":"priest","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":750},{"base":"H7239","lemma":"רִבּוֹ","tr":"rib·bo","gloss":"ten thousand","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":10},{"base":"H4349","lemma":"מָכוֹן","tr":"ma·khon","gloss":"foundation","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":17},{"base":"H5068","lemma":"נָדַב","tr":"na·dav","gloss":"be willing","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":17},{"base":"H5411","lemma":"נְתִינִים","tr":"na·tin","gloss":"temple servant","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":17},{"base":"H5892","lemma":"עִיר","tr":"ir","gloss":"excitement","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":1090},{"base":"H3801","lemma":"כֻּתֹּ֫נֶת","tr":"ke·to·net","gloss":"tunic","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":29}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"EXO","chapter":35,"verse":5,"verseEnd":19,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Take from among you an offering to the LORD. Let everyone whose heart is willing bring an offering to the LORD: gold, silver, and bronze; blue, purple, and scarlet yarn; fine linen and goat hair; ram skins dyed red and fine leather; acacia wood; olive oil for the light; spices for the anointing oil and for the fragrant incense; and onyx stones and gemstones to be mounted on the ephod and breastpiece.","from":68},{"book":"EXO","chapter":35,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So all the men and women of the Israelites whose hearts prompted them brought a freewill offering to the LORD for all the work that the LORD through Moses had commanded them to do.","from":68},{"book":"EXO","chapter":36,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"They received from Moses all the contributions that the Israelites had brought to carry out the service of constructing the sanctuary. Meanwhile, the people continued to bring freewill offerings morning after morning,","from":68},{"book":"NUM","chapter":7,"verse":3,"verseEnd":89,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"They brought as their offering before the LORD six covered carts and twelve oxen—an ox from each leader and a cart from every two leaders—and presented them before the tabernacle. And the LORD said to Moses, “Accept these gifts from them, that they may be used in the work of the Tent of Meeting. And give them to the Levites, to each man according to his service.” So Moses took the carts and oxen and gave them to the Levites. He gave the Gershonites two carts and four oxen, as their service required,","from":68},{"book":"1KI","chapter":7,"verse":51,"verseEnd":51,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So all the work that King Solomon had performed for the house of the LORD was completed. Then Solomon brought in the items his father David had dedicated—the silver, the gold, and the furnishings—and he placed them in the treasuries of the house of the LORD.","from":69},{"book":"1CH","chapter":11,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Even in times past, while Saul was king, you were the one who led Israel out and brought them back. And the LORD your God said, ‘You will shepherd My people Israel, and you will be ruler over them.’”","from":70},{"book":"1CH","chapter":21,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then the angel of the LORD ordered Gad to tell David to go up and build an altar to the LORD on the threshing floor of Ornan the Jebusite.","from":68},{"book":"1CH","chapter":22,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then David said, “Here shall be the house of the LORD God, as well as the altar of burnt offering for Israel.”","from":68}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]}}